A single run grows until the provider refuses it: every step appends the assistant message and every tool
result to the run's own message list, and only the *history* between runs is ever compressed. A long round —
a continuation, a build-fix loop — therefore ends with a context-length error instead of an answer.

Make the run compact its own messages when they cross the compression threshold, without losing the recent
steps it is reasoning about and without breaking tool calls: an assistant message with tool calls must stay
with the results that answer it.
